  message: "Done — both PRs merged, ADR-0042 §2 code-name migration. PR1 module rename (2ad2d3eb55, PR #647): behavior_map_io.py->survey_io.py + a deprecation shim (re-exports the 8 public names, warns on import). PR2 function rename (bcdffc5514, PR #650): cli.run_behavior_map->run_survey + a module-level alias (same object, identical signature). EVIDENCE: from hypergumbo_core.survey_io import load_substrate works; the behavior_map_io shim re-exports the same objects + fires DeprecationWarning on import (locked by test in test_survey_io.py); cli.run_survey canonical, run_behavior_map alias is-same-object with preserved signature so the ~56 test call-sites resolve unchanged. Internal src + loader test + bakeoff/analysis scripts migrated to survey_io. Both PRs 100% coverage on changed files. PROCESS LESSONS (durable): (1) a NEW standalone test file that is the SOLE coverer of a changed source file can be dropped from smart-test's committed manifest -> 0% coverage in CI's manifest run even though local smart-test (which runs new test files ad-hoc) shows 100%; fold such tests into an already-in-manifest file, or run check-package-coverage before pushing. (2) auto-pr's rebase silently clobbered an amend's working-tree edit when the branch was behind base; commit on an up-to-date base so auto-pr fast-forwards. RESIDUAL (window-close): call-site migration to run_survey (56 tests + few src) rides the deprecation window via the alias."  # 3dff
